  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative or neutral (sentiment ≤ 0.33) to counteract overconfidence.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes (last 5-7 days) when sentiment is positive (sentiment ≥ 0.50) to avoid lagging.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is > 10% above recent 30-day average, reduce by 5-10% unless sentiment strongly bullish.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp upward moves (e.g., >15% spike in 3-5 days) by 10-20% to prevent overcorrection.",
    "When sentiment is weak (0.00–0.33), use 30-day moving average as baseline; otherwise, weight sentiment more heavily in smoothing.",
    "For long-term (30-day) forecasts, penalize high variance in model output when sentiment is low; favor stability over volatility."
  ]
}
